<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Butua</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – 1683 CE (approx.) · capital Khami</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Torwa kingdom centred on Khami, heir to Great Zimbabwe in the south-west of the plateau and builder of richly decorated stone platforms.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Butua arose in the mid-15th century as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-zimbabwe">Kingdom of Zimbabwe</a> declined, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torwa-dynasty">Torwa dynasty</a> took control of the south-western plateau around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulawayo">Bulawayo</a>. Its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khami">Khami</a> continued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zimbabwe">Great Zimbabwe</a> building tradition, and the kingdom controlled gold-bearing lands and rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> pastures.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khami">Khami</a> was built on terraced stone platforms faced with chequered and herringbone patterns, a style later seen at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danangombe">Danangombe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naletale">Naletale</a>. Kings drew wealth from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and gold, trading with the Portuguese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> lands and the coast. Portuguese sources describe Butua as a rich gold country but give few details of its rulers or government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the mid-17th century a succession dispute brought in Portuguese allies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khami">Khami</a> was burnt. In the 1680s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changamire-dombo">Changamire Dombo</a>, a former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> herder-general, overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torwa-dynasty">Torwa</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> state on the same lands.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1450 CE – 1683 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.56%;width:4.64%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – 1683 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Khami</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Shona religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Shona (Kalanga)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>, <a href="/countries/botswana">Botswana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Torwa State, Butwa, Torwa dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1566&amp;focus=kingdom-of-butua" aria-label="Kingdom of Butua on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5446 2923 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Butua lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5766 3179L5791 3172M5766 3179L5834 3184"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5791 3172h0M5834 3184h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5766 3179h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5766 3179h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Khami. <a href="/atlas?year=1566&amp;focus=kingdom-of-butua">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
